- The integer array parameter `nums` is sorted in ascending order.
- The integer array parameter `nums` contains unique values.
- The length of the integer array parameter `nums` is less than or equal to 20.
- All values in the integer array parameter `nums` are greater than or equal to -2^31 and less than or equal to 2^31 - 1.
- The string list result contains the smallest sorted list of ranges that cover all the numbers in the array exactly.
- Each element of the integer array `nums` is covered by exactly one of the ranges in the string list result.
- If a range `[a,b]` in the list has `a` not equal to `b`, it is output as `"a->b"`.
- If a range `[a,b]` in the list has `a` equal to `b`, it is output as `"a"`.
- The string list result is in ascending order based on the starting values of the ranges.